<title>SRI LANKA: Lanka Lubricants nine-month net lower.</title>
<headline>Lanka Lubricants nine-month net lower.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited results of Lanka Lubricants Ltd for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of rupees unless stated):</p>
<p>		     9 months 1996	   9 months 1995</p>
<p>    Turnover	  1,539.48     vs	 1,316.93</p>
<p>    Net profit	   99.39     vs	   102.31</p>
<p>    tax provision	60.64     vs	    80.67</p>
<p>NOTE - Lanka Lubricants, which is Sri Lanka's monopoly lubricant oil maker, is a subsidiary of U.S. multi-national Caltex, which is a joint venture between Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp. --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
